# Agent Skills workflow

Before non-trivial technical work in this repo:

1. Route via `.agents/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md`.
2. Read and follow the matching skill under `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.
3. Read `CONSTRAINTS.md` before writing code — do not weaken it to make a change pass.
4. Prefer project skills over guessing; the user does not need to say "read skill" each time.

## Phase → skill (Khepree)

| Phase | Skill |
|-------|-------|
| New feature / phase | `spec-driven-development` → `planning-and-task-breakdown` |
| Implement | `incremental-implementation` |
| UI / marketing | `frontend-ui-engineering` |
| API / packages | `api-and-interface-design` |
| Auth / security | `security-and-hardening` |
| DB / migration | `deprecation-and-migration` |
| Tests | `test-driven-development` |
| Debug | `debugging-and-error-recovery` |
| Review | `code-review-and-quality` |
| Ship | `shipping-and-launch` |

Stack-specific rules live in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and the Khepree Master Prompt (inherit on every phase).
